  "summary": "Traditional blue and white ceramics from Modra, Slovakia featuring hand-painted floral and geometric patterns.",
  "description": "Modra ceramics are stoneware pieces decorated with distinctive blue floral and geometric patterns on white or cream backgrounds, created using a specialized cobalt glaze. This pottery tradition developed in the town of Modra in the 19th century, influenced by earlier folk pottery techniques but distinguished by its cobalt decoration and higher firing temperatures, which created durable tableware and decorative items that became symbols of Slovak cultural identity and craftsmanship.",
